      "pronunciationText": "That gives a short method. List the candidates: stationary points inside the interval, any interior points where f prime doesn't exist, and both endpoints. Then work out f at every one, and compare. Here, f prime of x is three, times x minus one, times x plus one. So the stationary points are minus one and one, both inside. The endpoints are minus two and three, and f prime exists everywhere. The values are minus two, two, minus two and eighteen. The largest is eighteen, so the global maximum is eighteen, at x equals three. The smallest is minus two, and it happens twice, at x equals minus two and x equals one. On the coaster, the highest point of this stretch is the top of the climb, not the hump, and the lowest point comes twice, at the start and in the dip. Notice we never had to classify anything. Comparing the values settles it."
    },
